# A failure union may name a type parameter beside an error the function owns
# (`(ShopError | E)!`), and each call reads it at its binding: `E = Never`
# leaves `ShopError` alone, `E = ShopError` adds nothing, `E = KeyError` joins
# it, and `E = ShopError | KeyError` adds no second `ShopError`. Each failure
# reaches the caller as the member it is, on every tier, whether the caller
# writes the union in the callee's member order, in its own, or nowhere.
fixture: GenericFailureUnionReadsItsBinding.fixture
step check: jet check main.jet
exit: 0
step run: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "3\n-1\n2\n-2\ntotal 5\nkey\nshop\nshop\nkey\ntotal 3\n2\n-4\n-5\n"
step o0: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == run
step o2: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == run
